# The shell's segments: where the root put them (KCALL_SEGMENT): its code in
# the image, its data and stack after the root's own, the OS server's, the
# drivers' and the transfer segments - above 1 MB where there is extended
# memory (Bochs, MAME: roadmap os-server.md P3), below it on DOSBox-X,
# which has none; limits from the CPU (LSL).
program: shell
keys: mem\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>mem
code:  selector 0007h, base 0{m:program.base}h, limit {m:program.limit}h
@bochs data:  selector 000Fh, base 126AF0h, limit 1FFFh
@bochs stack: selector 0017h, base 128AF0h, limit 07FFh
@mame data:  selector 000Fh, base 126AF0h, limit 1FFFh
@mame stack: selector 0017h, base 128AF0h, limit 07FFh
@dosbox-x data:  selector 000Fh, base 058050h, limit 1FFFh
@dosbox-x stack: selector 0017h, base 05A050h, limit 07FFh
Nothing else is reachable: the kernel's selectors fault here.
A:\>
